  contributed: Priest in Peril, Nature Spirit, Druidic Ritual, Bone Voyage, Tale of
  the Righteous, Cook's Assistant, Fairytale I, The Feud, Lost City, Swan Song,
  Monkey Madness I, Desert Treasure I, and 5 RFD pages) — left in scope per the
  brief's literal prefix list (questdb:*/quests:*) the study:multiquest-im:* rows that
  also touched Client of Kourend/Fairy ring, since that prefix wasn't named.
- Emitted 12 bundles (<=20 titles each): 9 quest-sweep chunks (180 remaining quests,
  alphabetically chunked — deliberately skipped thematic/region tagging from memory
  since bundle grouping is organizational metadata, not a wiki-sourced claim, and
  alphabetical chunking is deterministic/error-free vs guessed questline groupings),
  2 miniquest-sweep chunks (28), 1 diary-sweep bundle (12).
- Queued 3 wave4:* tickets (minigames, skill-unlocks, collection-log) per brief,
  payload-only, not bundled.
- CANONICAL-TRIGGER MINT: Category:<umbrella> is not a reliable "give me every X" source
  on this wiki — it silently mixes list/meta pages with real content pages and can omit
  real members from its own subcategories. Any future full-surface enumeration should
  budget for a 3-way union (umbrella category, minus known meta-page suffixes, union'd
  against the cleaner F2P/P2P-style subcategories) rather than trusting one members()
  call, and should verify a diary/achievement-style category exists before relying on it
  (Category:Achievement Diary returns empty; the real index is the article's own link list).

