## quests (classify) retro
- 191/191 quest rows classified, 0 skipped (contrib.jsonl had no prior "classify:quest"
  keys). kind="quest" + members=f2p/p2p are real (derived from category membership, the
  same filter the page's own DPL query uses); difficulty/length/qp/series are "??" for
  every row -- see [classify] gotcha, this is a structural wall not a shortcut.
- MAJOR FINDING: Quests/List (and its three transcluded sub-pages) render entirely via
  <dpl> extension queries -- zero literal quest data in wikitext, only the query
  definition. `get --strip` cannot help here; --strip removes noise from real content,
  it doesn't expand server-side templates. Confirmed by fetching Quests/Free-to-play.s2
  and Quests/Members.s2 directly (1038B/1256B of pure DPL config, no rows).
- Fell back to `members Category:Free-to-play quests` / `Category:Members' quests` to
  recover the real population + f2p/p2p split, since that's the exact filter the DPL
  itself queries on -- this is enumeration, not an individual-quest-page fetch, so it
  stays inside the hard limit while still being grounded in the page's actual query logic
  rather than guessed.
- Two correctness traps caught before writing rows: (1) Category:Members' quests
  includes "Recipe for Disaster/Full guide" (a guide meta-page, not a quest) which the
  real DPL explicitly excludes via `nottitlematch = %Full guide%`; (2) it also includes
  "Fallen From Grace" and "The Graveyard", both tagged Category:Future content (unreleased,
  DPL excludes via `notcategory = Future content`). Both caught by reading the DPL config
  text itself rather than trusting raw category membership.
- Did NOT touch Miniquests -- its DPL table has a different column set (no # or QP column,
  matching neither the task's described master-table columns nor a real quest), and a
  concurrent sibling classify agent's 28 "classify:<miniquest>" rows landed in contrib.jsonl
  during this run, confirming that was the right split.
- CANONICAL-TRIGGER MINT: when falling back to `members "Category:X"` because a page's
  table is DPL (per the miniquests-retro mint above), don't stop at raw category
  membership -- read the `<dpl>` block's own `notcategory=`/`nottitlematch=` lines first,
  they name real exclusions (meta pages the category over-includes, unreleased/Future
  content rows) that a plain member-list diff will silently miss and raw membership alone
  will get wrong.

